websocket bridge true
fiber poller true
wake alphabet ptxc same in latte.web true
-- 1. a real socket, on a port the kernel chose
ok 1.1 the first frame is a hello at wire v1
ok 1.2 the circuit id is 256 bits
ok 1.3 and hexadecimal

-- 2. attach mounts the page and sends batch 1
ok 2.1 the attach went out
ok 2.2 batch 1 is the whole page
ok 2.3 the ack went out

-- 3. a job posted from another OS thread reaches the wire
ok 3.1 batch 2 is the pushed value, and nothing else
ok 3.2 the ack went out

-- 4. a click is one text edit, not a page
ok 4.1 the click went out
ok 4.2 batch 3 updates one text node
ok 4.3 the ack went out

-- 5. an input event binds a field
ok 5.1 the input went out
ok 5.2 batch 4 writes the value attribute and the text that reads it
ok 5.3 the ack went out

-- 6. a keyed reorder MOVES a child, it does not rebuild the list
ok 6.1 the rotate click went out
ok 6.2 batch 5 is two relocates and the row-order text
ok 6.3 a second rotate went out
ok 6.4 batch 6 is two relocates again, from a different start
(batches 5 and 6 are left un-acked on purpose)

-- 7. the socket goes away
ok 7.1 the close handshake completed

-- 8. a new socket resumes the retained circuit and is replayed
ok 8.1 the new socket is a new circuit with its own id
ok 8.2 and it is NOT the one being resumed
ok 8.3 the resume went out
ok 8.4 batch 5 is replayed
ok 8.5 batch 6 is replayed
ok 8.6 the ack for the last replayed batch went out

-- 9. the page on the other end is the SAME page
ok 9.1 a click on the same handler id went out
ok 9.2 the count carried on from where it was
ok 9.3 a second bind went out
ok 9.4 pushed, bound and rotated state all came back
ok 9.5 the ack went out

-- 10. a handler panics and the circuit lives
ok 10.1 the boom click went out
ok 10.2 what the client is told is a trace id, never the message
ok 10.3 the boundary renders in its place

-- 11. a message the wire refuses ends the circuit politely
ok 11.1 a nonsense event name went out
ok 11.2 the last frame is a bye
ok 11.3 and the socket is finished

-- 12. what adoption refuses
ok 12.1 a resume naming a circuit that does not exist is forbidden
ok 12.2 a resume of THIS socket's own fresh circuit never attached
ok 12.3 and the same fresh socket attaches fine

39 checks, 0 bad

-- 13. the session binding, driven without a socket
ok 13.1 the circuit to be stolen is attached and has a page
ok 13.2 a resume from another session does not move the socket
ok 13.3 and the set says why
ok 13.4 the same resume from the right session moves the socket
ok 13.5 and the fresh circuit it arrived on is retired, not retained
ok 13.6 no second fault was recorded
6 checks, 0 bad

pages built 2 cross-thread post taken true
circuits still held 3 set faults 0
upgrades 5
